(text "Sheet 3: SC95F8523 controller, supplies and connectors. Pin numbers: SOP28/TSSOP28 (SinOne datasheet V0.3)." (at 25.4 30.48 0) (effects (font (size 2.0 2.0)) (justify left top)) (uuid 4781d606-d58f-5500-85b3-6bc6a5be3683))
(text "10 V gate-drive rail: Vout = 1.275 V x (1 + R7/R8) = 9.93 V.\nP0.5 (EN_10V) turns it on; R25 keeps it off during reset." (at 172.72 40.64 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left top)) (uuid 045040cd-4f69-5656-bea4-e2f77f5990bf))
(text "5 V logic rail, always on (15 uA quiescent).\nC31: use the ESR range in the LM2936 datasheet." (at 172.72 116.84 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left top)) (uuid c291af2e-1241-569f-aa9e-5d9ea0fbd695))
(text "NTC inputs: 100k pull-up, 10k B3950 NTC (off-board),\n12-bit ADC with 2.048 V reference." (at 320.04 137.16 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left top)) (uuid de1a55fa-67bb-509f-a330-e2c28f95f212))
(text "Notes\n- Unused pins P1.0, P0.6, P0.7 and PWM3: set as outputs driven low in firmware.\n- C25/C26: use the load capacitance from the crystal datasheet (typ. 10-15 pF).\n- Every ADC divider has 100 nF at the divider. Analog ground (dividers, NTCs, U5/U6) joins power ground at one point near R14.\n- J3: SinOne 2-wire programming (tCK/tDIO). J4: PIR / motion sensor. J5: service UART." (at 25.4 238.76 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left top)) (uuid 371f9589-73b5-5c17-8080-6369c0418d30))
)
